# Rust engine migration workflow

## Rule

Read [ENGINE_BOUNDARY.md](../../docs/ENGINE_BOUNDARY.md) first.

- **Engine** = port to `crates/*`, expose FFI, delete Dart equivalent, test.
- **Host** = `apps/forja` (Flutter permanent) — theme, WebView, player, OAuth.
- **No new engine logic in Dart** — port to `crates/*` when touching.

Only `packages/rust` survives under `packages/` long-term (FFI bridge).

**Wave 1 deletes:** `streaming`, `storage`, `core` (playback engine).
**Wave 2 deletes:** `packages/api`, `packages/kotlin` (catalog engine + cancelled Compose POC).

## Wave 1 exit gate

[Playback engine exit checklist](../../docs/migration/02-rust-engine-complete.md#playback-engine-exit-checklist) — app shippable; then start wave 2.

## Mandatory per engine port

1. Read Dart engine source.
2. Implement in matching `crates/<name>/`.
3. Add FFI in `crates/ffi` — **fetch+parse in Rust** (Pattern B).
4. Wire `apps/forja` to `ForjaEngine.*`.
5. **Delete the Dart slice** — directory, pubspec deps, imports.
6. **Tests** — Rust unit/golden + Dart parity in `packages/rust/test/parity/`.
7. Update [02-rust-engine-complete.md](../../docs/migration/02-rust-engine-complete.md) or [03-engine-catalog.md](../../docs/migration/03-engine-catalog.md).
8. Run `./scripts/build_rust.sh`, `cargo test --workspace`, `cd packages/rust && flutter test`.

## Never do

- Sync FFI on UI thread for resolve/search — use `Isolate.run` (P2-91)
- New Pattern A FFI (`*_html_json`) for engine work
- New engine logic in Dart
- Dart wrapper calling Rust instead of deleting Dart
- `*Backend` hooks, `rust_delegates.dart`

## Allowed

- Host orchestration for provider race UX (ENGINE_BOUNDARY R6)
- Legacy `packages/api` during wave 2 — no new Dart engine logic
- `Isolate.run` for long FFI calls
- Nuvio, WebView, WASM, player on host permanently

## Before coding

1. Read [docs/migration/README.md](../../docs/migration/README.md).
2. Active wave 1: [02-rust-engine-complete.md](../../docs/migration/02-rust-engine-complete.md).
3. Wave 2: [03-engine-catalog.md](../../docs/migration/03-engine-catalog.md).
4. Boundary: [ENGINE_BOUNDARY.md](../../docs/ENGINE_BOUNDARY.md).

## Doc status

- Flutter + Rust permanent — no UI framework migration.
- Wave 1 = playback engine normalized.
- Wave 2 = catalog engine normalized; only `packages/rust` remains.
